From: tribble@netcom.com (E. Dean Tribble)
Date: Thu, 20 Jan 1994 12:34:43 -0800
Subject: [94-1-342] Extropian love

	 Yes, Hayek was a believer in _evolved systems_. In _emergent
	 properties_, not necessarily deducible from simple axioms (at least
	 not in a way we can find, or have found so far).

In particular he was making the point that evolved systems embody much
knowledge that isn't apparent.  Thus, all the sexual taboos ( I had a
recent conversation on this) may serve inobvious but important
purposes, even though they seem really stupid.  A designed morality
will typically miss such subtle purposes, and thus end up with
pathologies that are hard to compensate for.  On the other hand, such
taboos might just be stupid.  There are certainly examples for which
the knowledge is extremely important.

dean

